  "notes": "Themes searched: independence and territory, language and culture, ethnic policy, government and leadership, economy, war and violence, communism and Russia, religion, foreign alliances. Government is split between the democratic Rada/Mikhnovsky line and the interwar integral line; economics has no common doctrine beyond a mixed economy in the OUN's plan. The old audit's pro-NATO/EU, China, hate-speech, surveillance and social-state answers were dropped as borrowing from governments' wider programmes. Strands answering differently: Svoboda and Right Sector and post-2014 parties are not sampled. Main gap: the OUN's own congress resolutions (1929, 1941, 1943), the Decalogue, Mikhnovsky's Samostiina Ukraina and Hrushevsky's writings could not be opened in full, so the integral strand rests on the Encyclopedia of Ukraine's account and Dontsov's translated book.",
